      "sourceTextSha256": "fa2b9e0073ff67bd1d8e10384e5a244141f2985eb216df228bfca17913f8da8e",
      "text": "Day 8 · After breakfast, a boat tour of an igapó, a flooded rainforest, where heavy rains turn the jungle into an enormous lake and unique aquatic plants and animals can be seen. Then try your hand at piranha fishing with a rod, and walk through the jungle to a caboclo community, a riverside people of mixed Indigenous and European heritage steeped in the history of the rainforest. Learn about the community’s origins, watch the preparation of manioc flour and discover traditional hunting techniques and the plants of the forest.",
